-- comments
1:1 plain -- A stray byte in a tag is one token that stops before the first `>`, `/`,
2:1 plain -- `{`, `}`, `"`, `=` or whitespace after it (frontend.md §9.1), so it
3:1 plain -- cannot swallow the tag's own syntax: `\` before `>` and `'s` before `>`
4:1 plain -- are one token each, each tag still ends at its `>`, and each stray is one
5:1 plain -- unexpected_token (8:8, 12:10). The markup is not_implemented at 8:5 and
6:1 plain -- 12:5.
